architecture broadcast
  source_lineage earliest source integrations/browser/narration-production.mjs first committed 2026-11-05 in 44c1481e "feat: land Aug 24 - Nov 5 native estate work"
  canonical_name Broadcast
  family surface
  domain Media / Produced audio programs
  layer surface
  semantic_question Given the item archive, the model estate's speech runtimes, the system's voices and open-licence archives, what produced audio programme can be made now, who speaks each line, what did each line cite, and what could not be voiced or played?
  purpose Native composer of produced audio programmes. A programme is a CUE clock (schemas/control/broadcast-programs.cue): desks read the freshest cited items of declared families or censuses, music and features cut open-terms excerpts from Internet Archive pools, idents speak over a ducked bed. Voices are cast from discovery, never named in code: neural runtimes over model-estate bodies verified by bonfyre model and loaded under an admission memory grant, the system's installed voices by locale, and speech providers whose key is present. The output is one programme audio file with Podcasting 2.0 chapters, a WebVTT transcript, credits with excerpt digests and a manifest of casts, fallbacks and skips, written as a draft MediaProgram.
  maturity implemented
  owns BroadcastProgramme
  owns BroadcastPlan
  owns BroadcastRender
  consumes KeptItem
  consumes MediaProgram
  publishes MediaProgram
  command BonfyreBroadcast
  internal_calculus cast roles onto discovered engines by kind preference, locale and distinctness; score desk candidates by recency plus log publisher depth, two lines per publisher, recurring dated columns dropped; open-terms check per excerpt at fetch time; loudness-normalised mixdown
