  source_path cmd/BonfyreBroadcast/tests/narration_assembly_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreBroadcast/tests/narration_assembly_test.sh checks a 64-take assembly plus gain, placement, a silent gap, transcript timing and a music mix; it refuses overlap and changed takes
  invariant native narration assembly admits at most 64 ordered non-overlapping takes and ten minutes, rechecks source hashes, and produces an exclusive WAV and escaped transcript for the editorial mixer
  invariant a browser assembly plan snapshots the production once and reuses the snapshot take buffers, so later edits cannot alter the prepared sources
  forbidden_inference a valid assembly plan -> reviewed scripts, authorized music or an approved publication
  known_gap the account arrangement can prepare a source-addressed assembly plan, but its UI does not yet submit retained production and blob identities to the native assembly service
  source_path cmd/BonfyreBroadcast/tests/editorial_mix_test.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/media_program.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/site_mcp.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/site_product_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreBroadcast/tests/editorial_mix_test.sh retains the v2 revision in a draft mix and refuses publication after structured source edits
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/site_product_test.sh checks current v2 recordings are shown and structured article edits hide stale audio
  invariant a v2-bound editorial mix carries the same published article revision through the draft media record and the public reader checks the current revision before exposing the recording
  witness cmd/BonfyreBroadcast/tests/article_revision_test.c checks public structured article revision identity, draft to published parity, duplicate subject refusal and namespace isolation
  invariant the v2 article revision hashes one bounded database snapshot of public editor data and keeps existing media source fingerprints unchanged
  forbidden_inference an article revision fingerprint -> reviewed narration, music rights, or publication
  known_gap legacy source fingerprints do not cover structured editor content; v2-bound drafts require the CMS media revision field and do not by themselves produce or publish narration
  source_path cmd/BonfyreBroadcast/Makefile
  source_path schemas/control/broadcast-programs.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreBroadcast/tests/broadcast_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreBroadcast/tests/broadcast_test.sh: offline fixture archive and fixed engines; casting honours readiness, preference, locale and distinctness; the empty desk is dropped and recorded; two lines per publisher; future, stale and recurring-column items excluded; one title once; every desk line cites source, key and href; publish writes one draft row idempotently and never a publication (make -C cmd/BonfyreBroadcast test PASS, 2026-11-08)
  witness 2026-11-08 real render of estate-hour against ~/.bonfyre/estate-local/items.db (88,531 items): 545.8 s programme, 39 spoken lines, 6 open-licence excerpts (netlabel CC BY / BY-SA, NASA public domain, LibriVox public domain), 12 chapters, integrated loudness -16.8 LUFS; whisper read the opening back intelligibly. The neural anchor was deferred by admission (spendable memory) and the manifest records 11 fallbacks to system voices
  invariant every desk line carries the source, key and href of the item it reads
  invariant an excerpt plays only when its source states public domain, CC0, CC BY or CC BY-SA at fetch time; anything else is skipped and recorded
  invariant a neural speech load takes a memory grant first; a refused grant falls back and is recorded, never loads into swap
  invariant a neural line is kept only when whisper's read-back recall meets the runtime's floor
  invariant publish writes a draft; publication and hosting are the owner's
  forbidden_inference a spoken headline -> the story is true, current or endorsed; it repeats the item's title and names its publisher and date
  forbidden_inference an excerpt's stated licence -> a clearance; it is what the Archive item stated when fetched
  forbidden_inference read-back recall -> voice quality, naturalness or fitness for broadcast
  forbidden_inference a draft MediaProgram -> a published, hosted or scheduled episode
  forbidden_inference a cast engine -> consent of any person to have their voice imitated; engines are synthetic and named in the manifest
  known_gap the item archive's major newsrooms stop on 2026-09-19 (news) and 2026-10-19 (today, money, local-news); programmes read what is there, so the headlines desk is a month old until those reads resume
  known_gap the neural runtime has been exercised directly (llama-tts, OuteTTS 0.3 500M, 6.1 s line, whisper read-back) but not inside a render: two publish-pass memory grants from 2026-11-01 and 2026-11-03 were still open with no expiry and the ledger deferred it
  known_gap a draft MediaProgram is not yet attached to an AccountWorldAudio station or show (episode, chapter, source and track marks, WebVTT cues); that needs a world, a space and a hosted https asset, and hosting runs through the owner's edge publish
  known_gap OuteTTS speaks with its default speaker only; per-role neural voices need speaker profiles, and Kokoro or provider voices are declared but absent here (no loopback server, no key)
  known_gap the closing credit is spoken by a system voice and says the licence family, not the exact licence version, which is in the credits

interaction broadcast-casts-model-estate-speech
  source broadcast
  destination model-commons
  relation speech_runtime_binding_to_verified_body_under_memory_grant
  preserves the model and vocoder ids, their verified digests, the runtime's licence and the admission verdict for each load
  drops any engine whose body is absent or unverified, and any load the ledger defers
  forbidden_inference a registered speech model -> an admitted load, or voice quality
  invalidates_on model bytes, vocoder bytes, runtime binary or admission policy changing
  witness cmd/BonfyreBroadcast/tests/broadcast_test.sh
  binding cmd/BonfyreBroadcast/src/main.c

interaction broadcast-reads-item-archive
  source broadcast
  destination item-archive
  relation cited_item_selection_to_spoken_line
  preserves source, key, href, publisher and date of every item read aloud
  drops items dated in the future, outside the desk window, repeated titles and recurring dated columns
  forbidden_inference a selected item -> its story is the day's most important
  invalidates_on the item archive, the census source lists or the scoring rule changing
  witness cmd/BonfyreBroadcast/tests/broadcast_test.sh
  binding cmd/BonfyreBroadcast/src/main.c
